{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"A6-0d oracle card (strong-tier, pre-code). Authoritative contract: current signed ticket plan plus Git bundle/ref semantics exercised through stock Git. Existing coverage inventory: A6-0c covers shared Git subprocess and partial-clone refusal, but repository search found no bundle-create/verify/restore or reclaim-backup tests. Preconditions: clean full unfiltered clone; origin exposes tickets plus ancestor/descendant/diverged/unrelated heads, annotated tag, lightweight blob tag; old tip equals initial remote tickets OID; output paths are absent and outside registered worktrees/Git dirs. Production path: CLI -> exact ls-remote snapshot/de-peel -> local object/type and ancestry classification -> explicit temporary refs -> bundle create/verify -> JSON manifest -> restore probe -> exact remote snapshot comparison -> owned cleanup. Tier: real temporary Git remotes/worktrees/subprocesses; a unit tier cannot prove ref reachability, bundle headers, restore, or no remote mutation. Exact postconditions: manifest inventory/relationships exact, bundle named OID map exact, restore map exact, remote bytes unchanged, no push/delete, outputs atomic/no-overwrite. Recovery: injected bundle-verify failure removes owned outputs/refs and same-clone retry succeeds; simulated abnormal state is refused and a fresh-clone retry succeeds. Contention: exempt from rebar shared-store suites because the helper owns one offline fresh clone and never mutates the ticket store; no cross-clone shared state exists. Surface census: CLI in scope via real subprocess; library facade and MCP/API out of scope for one-time ops; A6-1 automated caller is deferred but consumes the same CLI; dual direction in scope through create+restore. Gate: exact integration node, then make lint/typecheck/test. Implementer tier: standard/mid because Git graph classification, atomic artifacts, and recovery span one production file and one integration harness; only the happy path will remain visible."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785849675350236001,"uuid":"069e1ccb-7dfc-418f-9b32-71aff565d92c"}